From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonas Köppeler <j.koeppeler@tu-berlin.de>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:43:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net/sched: sch_cake: fix unintended tin override with cake_mq

CAKE permits a skb->priority tin override when its major number matches
the qdisc handle. cake_mq creates its child CAKE qdiscs without handles,
so their handle is zero. Forwarded IPv4 traffic can have skb->priority
rewritten from TOS by ip_forward_update_priority (enabled by default),
which can accidentally match that zero handle and bypass DSCP tin
selection.

For a shared cake_mq child, compare against the major number of the
parent cake_mq handle instead. Plain CAKE keeps using its own handle.

This is important for diffserv4 classification of forwarded traffic.
For example, AF41 should enter the Video tin, not be reclassified through
the legacy skb->priority override.

Link: https://lkml.rescloud.iu.edu/hypermail/linux/kernel/2611.2/12378.html
Fixes: ebc65a873eff ("net/sched/sch_cake: Add cake_mq qdisc for using cake on mq devices")
Signed-off-by: Jonas Köppeler <j.koeppeler@tu-berlin.de>
---
 net/sched/sch_cake.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/net/sched/sch_cake.c
+++ b/net/sched/sch_cake.c
@@ -1679,7 +1679,7 @@ static struct cake_tin_data *cake_select_tin(struct Qdisc *sch,
 {
 	struct cake_sched_data *qd = qdisc_priv(sch);
 	struct cake_sched_config *q = qd->config;
-	u32 tin, mark;
+	u32 tin, mark, handle;
 	bool wash;
 	u8 dscp;

@@ -1689,6 +1689,8 @@ static struct cake_tin_data *cake_select_tin(struct Qdisc *sch,
 	 */
 	mark = (skb->mark & q->fwmark_mask) >> q->fwmark_shft;
 	wash = !!(q->rate_flags & CAKE_FLAG_WASH);
+	handle = q->is_shared ? TC_H_MAJ(sch->parent) : sch->handle;
+
 	if (wash)
 		dscp = cake_handle_diffserv(skb, wash);

@@ -1698,7 +1700,7 @@ static struct cake_tin_data *cake_select_tin(struct Qdisc *sch,
 	else if (mark && mark <= qd->tin_cnt)
 		tin = qd->tin_order[mark - 1];

-	else if (TC_H_MAJ(skb->priority) == sch->handle &&
+	else if (TC_H_MAJ(skb->priority) == handle &&
 		 TC_H_MIN(skb->priority) > 0 &&
 		 TC_H_MIN(skb->priority) <= qd->tin_cnt)
 		tin = qd->tin_order[TC_H_MIN(skb->priority) - 1];

--
2.43.0
